inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point lies *on* the $y$-axis, $9$ units *below* the origin in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $0,$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-9.$\n\nTherefore, its coordinates are $(0,-9).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426969 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426969 #edb/ref 1069 "q-22349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426969 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426969 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shows the point $A(-3,4)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426969 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22c2c4da-83e3-5354-8e45-5160f1d5290b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426969 #edb/ref 1074 "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $A.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $A$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3,$ so we move $3$ units to the *left*, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $A$ has a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units *up*, in the *positive* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/d5/d5143459ae5b0e9704d8faa67dd3acf429832b668eae21ef9ca9e031e551432f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426970 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426970 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5752" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426970 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426970 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fe/fe8c79d8a237eab897b0ceea7ab4d4cf9a907360660c223d7486f8e3c5a18958.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426970 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2b4a8301-d80d-5d6b-b666-4d13d2e8333a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426970 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point lies *on* the $y$-axis, $1$ unit *below* the origin in